    <DataNode elementId="AT5G49970-MONOMER" textLabel="pyridoxamine-phosphate oxidase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LTX3" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding pyridoxine (pyridoxamine) 5&apos;-phosphate oxidase (AtPPOX), the bifunctional enzyme catalyzing the oxidative conversion of both pyridoxamine 5&apos;-phosphate (PMP) and pyridoxine 5&apos;-phosphate (PNP) to pyridoxal 5&apos;-phosphate (PLP) has been identified and partially characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The molecular function of the enzyme was confirmed by characterizing the recombinant protein expressed in and purified from &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; as well as through functional complementation of a PPOX knock-out mutant of yeast |CITS: [17224143]|.</Comment>
